-- title:
--   $(\mathbf{Q}\to\mathbf{Q}/\mathbf{Z})\times\mathrm{id}_{\mathbf{Q}}$ is not a quotient map: a product of quotient maps need not be a quotient map
-- statement:
--   The classical example showing that a product of two quotient maps of topological spaces need not be a quotient map.
--
--   Let $\mathbf{Q}$ carry the subspace topology of the Euclidean topology of $\mathbf{R}$. Let $X'=\mathbf{Q}/\mathbf{Z}$ be the quotient *space* obtained from $\mathbf{Q}$ by identifying the subset of integers $\mathbf{Z}\subset\mathbf{Q}$ to a single point (this is not the quotient group), with the quotient topology, and let $f:\mathbf{Q}\to X'$ be the quotient map. A map is a *quotient map* (*submersive* in the source) if it is surjective and a subset of the target is open if and only if its preimage is open.
--
--   **Statement.** The map
--   $$f\times\mathrm{id}_{\mathbf{Q}}:\mathbf{Q}\times_0\mathbf{Q}\longrightarrow X'\times_0\mathbf{Q},\qquad (x,y)\longmapsto(f(x),y),$$
--   where both sides carry the product topology, is not a quotient map.
--
--   The map $f\times\mathrm{id}_{\mathbf{Q}}$ is continuous and surjective, so the assertion is that there is a subset of $X'\times_0\mathbf{Q}$ which is not open although its preimage in $\mathbf{Q}\times_0\mathbf{Q}$ is open. The example shows that the stability of quotient maps under products, valid in the category of compactly generated spaces for the $k$-ified products, fails in the category of all topological spaces; it also yields that $X'\times_0\mathbf{Q}$ is neither compactly generated nor sequential (Example E.1.2.24 of the paper).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The space $X'$ is `Quot r` for the relation `r x y := ∃ m n : ℤ, x = m ∧ y = n` on `ℚ`; `Quot r` is the quotient by the equivalence relation generated by `r`, which identifies two rationals exactly when they are equal or both integers, and Mathlib endows it with the quotient topology. `ℚ` has its usual (metric) topology and both product types carry the product topology, which is the default instance.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, draft of 20 November 2026, https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf, p. 842, Example E.1.2.18; classical reference (as cited by the paper): R. Brown, Topology and Groupoids: a Geometric Account of General Topology, Homotopy Types and the Fundamental Groupoid, Createspace (2006), Ch. 4, Example 4

import Mathlib

open Topology TopologicalSpace

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace CGSpace

theorem not_isQuotientMap_prodMap_id_rat :
    ¬ IsQuotientMap
      (Prod.map (Quot.mk (fun x y : ℚ => ∃ m n : ℤ, x = m ∧ y = n)) (id : ℚ → ℚ)) := by sorry

end CGSpace
